A few general remarks on your playing style (from a heavily spoiled
source-diver):

We say that the DevTeam thinks of everyting, but that is not true. I get
the impression that you base decisions sometimes on the feeling that it
would be somehow right for things to work a particular way, whithout
having checked it (I'm being vague here, lest you get spoiled). Go and
ask yourself whether you have actually seen supporting evidence on your
view of the game mechanics, behaviour of creatures etc.

Furthermore, it would help your progress much if you learn to identify
things as early as possible. In particular for wands there are very easy
and precise ways to identify the various kinds, and it's not too hard to
figure it out.

